    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0247" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-28T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1925—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Referring to Department’s 398 of November 8,<anchor n="40" xml:id="d141-f1"/>
                    Standard Oil Company has again brought to attention of Department the matter of
                    your endeavoring to persuade British Government to instruct Bradbury to vote for
                    a compromise on tanker question. Logan<anchor n="41" xml:id="d141-f2"/> informs
                    Department that you are now endeavoring to obtain agreement of <pb facs="0248"
                        n="166" xml:id="pg166"/> British Government before January 30 meeting of
                    Reparation Commission. You may continue to assist the company in such ways as
                    are possible and proper in the present circumstances. Logan has been so
                    informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
